## 5. Property Vocabulary

### 5.1 Provenance Properties (All Nodes)

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| as_of | date | Date the assertion was valid |
| source | string | Who asserted it (role and, where relevant, name) |
| confidence | enum | high, medium, low |
| confidentiality | enum | routine, restricted |

### 5.2 Clinical Properties (CLN.PT)

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| diagnosis | string | Clinical diagnosis |
| medication | string | Medication name and dose |
| contraindication | string | Contraindicated drug, treatment, or activity |
| mode-match | string | Context in which a functional claim holds |
| current_setting | enum | hospital, skilled-nursing, home, other |
| admission_date | date | Date of admission to current setting |
| admitting_diagnosis | string | Reason for admission |
| functional_note | string | Narrative qualifier on a functional-status node |
| status | enum | active, resolved, held, monitoring |

### 5.3 Care-Team Properties (CLN.CARE)

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| role | string | Clinical or advocacy role |
| contact | string | Contact channel (restricted) |
| authority | string | Scope of decision authority (e.g. power of attorney) |
| stated-position | string | The actor's asserted stance on a contested question |

### 5.4 Evidence Properties (CLN.EVID)

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| channel | enum | in-person, phone, portal, letter, care-conference |
| observed-by | string | Clinician or party who made the observation |
| contradicts | reference | Node id this observation or position contradicts |
| disposition | enum | open, escalated, resolved, withdrawn |

---

## 6. Domain-Specific Edge Types

| Type | Layer | Description |
|------|-------|-------------|
| cln.CONTRADICTS | semantic | One position or observation contradicts another; both retained |
| cln.SUPERSEDES_CLINICALLY | temporal | A newer observation supersedes an older one for the same measure |
| cln.CONDITIONAL_ON | causal | A functional claim holds only in a stated mode or condition |
| cln.RISK_OF | causal | A problem or diagnosis creates a risk |
| cln.MITIGATED_BY | causal | A risk is mitigated by an order, intervention, or precaution |
| cln.ASSERTED_BY | entity | A clinical node is attributed to a care-team actor |
| cln.EVIDENCED_BY | semantic | A clinical assertion is backed by an observation or document |
| cln.GATES | causal | A gate node blocks a transition until criteria are met |

---

## 7. Document Type Tags

| Tag | Description |
|-----|-------------|
| PATIENT | Patient record document (problems, meds, functional status) |
| CARE-TEAM | Care-team and institutional-actor roster |
| OBSERVATION | Time-indexed clinical observation set |
| COMMS | Communications log |
| CONFLICT | Dispute and administrative-proceeding record |
| GOALS | Care goals and discharge gates |
| RESTRICTED | Contains protected health information (excluded from uncleared traversal) |

---

## 8. Confidence Methodology

Confidence is a required, coarse-grained annotation (`high`, `medium`, `low`) rather than a numeric score, because clinical certainty is rarely quantifiable at the point of assertion.

- **high** — directly observed by a clinician, or documented in the chart
- **medium** — reported second-hand, or inferred from consistent indirect evidence
- **low** — single unverified source, or an assertion in active dispute

Confidence decays with staleness: a functional-status node more than one care-setting transition old is downgraded until re-observed. A node in an open `CONFLICT-` is capped at `medium` regardless of source, because the contradiction is itself evidence of uncertainty.

---

## 9. Temporal Semantics

### 9.1 Time-Indexing

Every clinical assertion carries `as_of`. A traversal engine SHOULD prefer the most recent assertion for a given measure and SHOULD flag any assertion whose `as_of` predates the current care setting's admission.

### 9.2 Clinical Supersession

When a newer observation replaces an older one for the same measure, a `cln.SUPERSEDES_CLINICALLY` edge is created and the older node is retained with `status: resolved` or `status: monitoring`. The record preserves what was believed and when.

### 9.3 Mode-Qualified Validity

A functional claim carrying `mode-match` is valid only within its stated mode. Two mode-qualified claims about the same function are not a contradiction unless they share a mode.

---

## 10. Traversal Policy

```yaml
traversal:
  default_entry_points: ["PT-PROFILE"]
  primary_layers: [temporal, causal]
  focus_areas:
    profile:
      entry: ["PT-PROFILE"]
      layers: [entity, semantic]
      keywords: ["patient", "baseline", "who", "overview"]
    problems:
      entry: ["PROB-INDEX"]
      layers: [causal, semantic]
      keywords: ["problem", "diagnosis", "condition", "risk"]
    medications:
      entry: ["MED-INDEX"]
      layers: [semantic]
      keywords: ["medication", "drug", "dose", "contraindication", "held"]
    functional:
      entry: ["FUNC-INDEX"]
      layers: [temporal, causal]
      keywords: ["function", "mobility", "ambulation", "adl", "mode"]
    disposition:
      entry: ["GOAL-INDEX", "GATE-INDEX"]
      layers: [causal]
      keywords: ["goal", "discharge", "gate", "transition", "home"]
    conflicts:
      entry: ["CONFLICT-INDEX"]
      layers: [semantic, temporal]
      keywords: ["conflict", "dispute", "contradiction", "appeal", "disagreement"]
    evidence:
      entry: ["OBS-INDEX", "COMM-INDEX"]
      layers: [semantic, temporal]
      keywords: ["observation", "communication", "source", "document", "evidence"]
```

---

## 11. Corpus Structure (Per-Patient)

```
<patient>/
├── RESTRICTED-*.md                    # Protected identifiers, contacts (excluded from traversal)
├── record/                            # CLN.PT
│   ├── 01-profile.lts                 # PT- nodes
│   ├── 02-problems.lts                # PROB-, DX-, RISK- nodes
│   ├── 03-medications.lts             # MED-, ORD- nodes
│   ├── 04-functional-status.lts       # FUNC- nodes (mode-qualified)
│   └── 05-goals-gates.lts             # GOAL-, GATE- nodes
├── care-team/                         # CLN.CARE
│   ├── 10-providers.lts               # CLIN- nodes
│   ├── 11-family-advocates.lts        # FAM- nodes
│   └── 12-institutions.lts            # FACIL-, POS- nodes
├── evidence/                          # CLN.EVID
│   ├── 20-observations.lts            # OBS- nodes
│   ├── 21-communications.lts          # COMM- nodes
│   ├── 22-documents.lts               # DOC- nodes
│   └── 23-conflicts.lts               # CONFLICT- nodes
├── events/
│   └── quality.jsonl                  # Quality event stream
└── deltas/
    └── DELTA-{date}-{short-sha}.lts
```

---

## 12. Why This Domain Exercises the Format

The clinical domain stresses parts of the format that first-party technical domains do not:

1. **Provenance and confidence are load-bearing, not decorative** — every assertion has a source and a certainty because the record must survive disagreement between actors.
2. **Contradiction is a first-class edge** — the format holds incompatible positions with equal fidelity rather than forcing resolution on write.
3. **Mode qualification** — a distinct temporal/conditional mechanism (`mode-match`, `cln.CONDITIONAL_ON`) that other domains rarely need.
4. **Confidentiality as structure** — restricted nodes are excluded from traversal by construction, demonstrating access control at the graph layer.

A format that encodes both a software architecture and a contested patient discharge with the same structural discipline is domain-agnostic in fact, not just in claim.

